Modifications to deck.gl as redistributed by Zebflow
====================================================

What is here
------------

  0.1/runtime/deckgl.bundle.mjs    an upstream deck.gl build
  0.1/runtime/deckgl.patched.mjs   Zebflow's wrapper, which imports the above

The file named "patched" is a Zebflow wrapper around the bundle, not an edit of
deck.gl's source. It adds layer construction from a declarative spec, tooltip
handling, and instance bookkeeping. deck.gl's own code is imported, not altered.

Network behaviour left as upstream ships it
-------------------------------------------

The bundle carries three CDN references, all upstream defaults:

  https://unpkg.com/@loaders.gl/...    worker bundles for binary formats
  https://unpkg.com/webgl-debug@2.0.1  only when WebGL debug mode is enabled
  https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/spectorjs  only when the debug-spectorjs flag is set

None is reached by the Studio. It uses PathLayer, PolygonLayer,
ScatterplotLayer and TileLayer, which take plain arrays and GeoJSON and parse
in-thread. The loaders.gl CDN is a fallback for formats none of those need.

This is dormant, not removed. A future layer taking a binary format would fetch
from unpkg, and would fail on a machine with no network. If that day comes, the
fix is to vendor the needed @loaders.gl worker and point loaders.gl at it —
not to discover it in the field.
